From fb997e62174368720901d4af7a8b312f5970f68f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tobias <ruck.tobias@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 1 May 2021 15:47:59 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 091/196] New Lotus block header (#151)

Updates the block header layout and hashing:
- Multi-layered block hashing allowing different levels of validation
- Block size for rejecting oversized blocks early on
- Block height for cheap DAA verification, and for smart contracts
- 5040 block epoch for smart contracts and sparse block header validation
- Extended metadata for adding metadata to block headers in a canonical way
- Widens the time to 6 bytes to delay the 2106 Problem by around 8M years
- Widens nonce to 8 bytes for simplified pool operations
- Shrinks block version to 1 byte and enforces versions as consensus
- Reduce the powLimit by approx. 16x to make it an even power of 2 for a later subsidy change
